        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": [],
          "text": "{\"occurrence_id\":\"bronte-tenant-of-wildfell-hall-14275eeb09f3d72c\",\"core_classification\":{\"label_support\":{\"truth_conditional\":3,\"performative\":4,\"exclamatory_reflexive\":0,\"other\":0},\"confidence\":0.95,\"analysis\":\"Helen’s conditional future declaration both avows an existing love that can become greater and, more strongly, offers renewed or intensified love as a relational undertaking contingent on Arthur’s perseverance in sobriety. The tearful, emphatic delivery does not independently make the words an expressive/reflex-like discharge.\",\"ambiguity\":\"The future form can be heard partly as a prediction about Helen’s feelings and partly as a promise or pledged reward; the exhortative conditional context strongly favors substantial performative force alongside avowal.\"},\"other_diagnosis\":{\"tpe_failure\":null,\"core_not_context\":null},\"utterance_status\":{\"status\":\"direct\",\"description\":\"Helen directly addresses Arthur; the speech event is reproduced as dialogue within her written diary narrative.\"},\"contextual_interpretation\":\"Helen is elated by what she takes to be Arthur’s renewed temperance and affection. She uses the declaration to encourage him to maintain his good resolutions, making intensified love both an avowed emotional prospect and an incentive-like relational promise. Her being “overflowing with affection,” squeezing him, and crying in “tearful earnest” establishes emotional intensity and sincerity as she understands them, but does not by itself supply independent expressive/reflexive force. The surrounding narrative also suggests hopeful idealisation, without changing the utterance’s T/P classification.\",\"evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"e1\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“Do, do persevere! and I’ll love you better than ever I did before!”\",\"supports\":\"The imperative and conditional coordination frame intensified love as an undertaking or promised consequence intended to encourage Arthur’s perseverance.\",\"confidence\":0.98},{\"evidence_id\":\"e2\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"Helen says she has come to thank Arthur for “temperance and sobriety” and asks him not to be laughed or grumbled out of his “good resolutions” or affection for her.\",\"supports\":\"The declaration functions within an appeal for continued sobriety and relational fidelity, strongly supporting performative force.\",\"confidence\":0.97},{\"evidence_id\":\"e3\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"The narrator describes herself as “so light of heart, so overflowing with affection” and later says she spoke in “tearful earnest.”\",\"supports\":\"This supports a sincere, emotionally intense avowal but, absent evidence of involuntary blurting or verbal discharge, does not independently support E.\",\"confidence\":0.94},{\"evidence_id\":\"e4\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“better than ever I did before” presupposes that Helen has loved Arthur previously and presents future love as an increase.\",\"supports\":\"The comparative construction supplies substantial truth-conditional presentation of Helen’s loving state across past, present, and anticipated future.\",\"confidence\":0.96},{\"evidence_id\":\"e5\",\"source\":\"supplied_metadata\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"The supplied form metadata classifies the occurrence as affirmative future tense/aspect.\",\"supports\":\"The future construction is compatible with prediction but, in this exhortative context, reinforces the reading as a prospective relational undertaking.\",\"confidence\":0.95}],\"background_knowledge\":{\"used\":false,\"familiarity\":\"none\",\"confidence\":null,\"contribution\":null},\"ontology_assessment\":{\"fit\":\"natural\",\"diagnosis\":\"T and P naturally capture the core force: an avowal of love combined with a conditional pledge of intensified love. Emotional delivery is adequately treated as context, leaving no important residual core force for E or O.\",\"candidate_recurrent_dimension\":null},\"notes\":null}"
